    "answer": {
      "short": "22; the two-digit multiples of 4 run from $4\\times3=12$ to $4\\times24=96$.",
      "worked": "The first two-digit multiple of 4 is $4\\times3=12$, and the last is $4\\times24=96$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Number of multiples}&=24-3+1\\\\&=22\\end{align*}$$",
